 {:the-gap
  "P-validated-R5.md:488 states F4 as: `for a given tension there is at least one
   pattern in the repository the finder must NOT return (a zero-mass pattern --
   T1512Z applied to retrieval); a finder that can return anything for anything
   is unfalsifiable.` Two formalisations of that sentence are already in the tree
   and they are not equivalent. READING A, FindFalsifiable
   (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:31), takes the excluded
   pattern from the FINDER'S OWN OUTPUT: forall t repo, repo nonempty ->
   exists p in repo.patterns, p not in (f t repo).selected. READING B,
   FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/
   F11DischargeArm.lean:59), takes it from the RECORD: the patterns
   futon3 checks/find_snatch.clj:25-31 declared zero-mass in advance are in the
   repository and out of the selection. Slice 2 refuted A of the record's own
   replay (F11Conformance.lean:207); slice 3 refuted B of a finder that satisfies
   A (F11DischargeArm.lean:207). Neither entails the other."
  :expected-third-reading
  "The paper's `must not` is DEONTIC -- the designation of which pattern is
   zero-mass comes from outside the finder, and reading A is the existential
   collapse of it in which the finder is allowed to nominate the excluded pattern
   AFTER the fact. Expected: a reading parameterised by a zero-mass designation
   zm : State -> Set P, of which reading B is the instance at the RECORDED
   designation, is what the sentence literally says, and reading A is strictly
   weaker than it at every designation. If that is wrong -- if reading A fails to
   follow from the parameterised form -- that is the measurement, not a defect.
   Written here before the result so it cannot be back-fitted."
  :expected-conjunction-cost
  "A and B are expected to PULL IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS on this record, so that
   requiring both costs the record's own selections. A asks the finder to exclude
   something from EVERY repository, singletons included; the recorded replay
   returns the whole of a repository holding only askForSurplusNotSurrender,
   which every recorded scenario selects (F11Conformance.lean:207). B asks it to
   exclude patterns that differ BY SCENARIO -- findSnatchZeroMass
   (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:342-348) takes THREE distinct values
   over the six scenarios: consultTheRemedyBeforeExiting at g1Snatcher, g1Sharer,
   g1Cautious and g2Snatcher, forcedPlayNeedsALossFloor at g4Snatcher,
   reEnterAfterObservedRepair at g5Sharer -- so no single fixed exclusion
   satisfies B across the six. Expected: on this record the
   only finders satisfying A AND B are ones that drop recorded selections on some
   input, findRefusing among them, and the conjunction arm's cost is therefore
   that a conformant find can no longer replay the record. If a finder is found
   that satisfies both AND reproduces every recorded selection, the expectation is
   refuted and THAT is the slice's finding."
  :inhabitance-floor-demanded-in-advance
  "C561 section 7b records that six consecutive slices across :F11/:F12 needed
   review to supply the same floor -- an agreement or disagreement claim witnessed
   by a finder that excludes everything carries nothing, because one side of the
   agreement is vacuous. C561 also records that ASKING for the floor in the packet
   was not sufficient last time. So this packet states the floor as a property of
   the witnesses rather than as an instruction: every claim that two readings
   agree, disagree, or are ordered must be witnessed by finders that SELECT at
   least one pattern on the recorded 18-pattern findSnatchRepository, and each
   such witness must carry a theorem that its selection there is nonempty.
   findRefusing and findSilent may appear only as the cheap-inhabitant baseline,
   never as a side of an agreement."}
